    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The largest empire in history, ruling roughly a quarter of the world's people at its peak around 1920.</li><li>Naval supremacy, industrial power and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#london">City of London</a> spread its laws, parliaments and language worldwide.</li><li>Two world wars drained its wealth; after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#indian-independence">Indian independence</a> in 1947 it dissolved within a few decades.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#indian-civil-service">Indian Civil Service</a> ran a country of some 300 million people with a cadre of only about 1,000 to 1,200 senior officers.</p></aside>
    </section>

